+# Crowd control inside non-raid dungeons: there is no config key for this, the
+# behavior is always on. The generic per-class "cc" strategies do not fire
+# while the bot is in a non-raid dungeon, so bots will not cast their generic
+# CC spells (Polymorph, Shackle Undead, Turn Undead, Scare Beast, Hibernate,
+# Freezing Trap, Sap, Entangling Roots, Banish, Fear) on dungeon trash - a
+# CC'd mob that breaks out early aggros nearby packs and can wipe the group.
+# Dungeon instance strategies keep their own named CC, and open world, raids
+# and battlegrounds keep generic CC. Ported from mod-playerbots PR #2648.
+# Implementation-verified, gameplay-untested.
+
 # Percentage of fully active bots. Default is 10, higher numbers may affect performance
 # AiPlayerbot.botActiveAlone = 10
 
